SAANICH, British Columbia — ABB Ltd (NYSE and SIX: ABB, “ABB” or the “Company”) announced today that it will hold its Annual General Meeting of Shareholders on Friday, May 2, 2019, at 8:00 a.m. local time at its offices at Corporate Tower (20 (370) Tillson Building in Vancouver, Canada) under the chairmanship of Mr. Thierry Breton.
ABB’s President and Chief Executive Officer, Mr. Ulrich Spiesshofer, and the following listed officers of the Company will be present at the AGM. This list of directors and officers will remain in effect, unless someone submits a requisition for the meeting, which the Company is reviewing. The meeting will be recorded and webcast live.
Investors and analysts can access the live webcast by visiting www.abb.com/abb_webcast.php . A replay of the webcast will be available within 2 days following the conclusion of the event.
ABB is a global technology leader providing power and automation technologies that make utilities and industry more sustainable, electrifying clean energy and powering smart grids.
At ABB, we are more than engineers. We bring the digital world to life with our digital solutions and resilient, reliable solutions for a range of customer needs – in Utility, Industry, Power Systems and Automation. We engineer and manufacture products for customers around the world, including a leading-edge products portfolio for electrification of energy sources, the need for electric mobility, power distribution and controls for the smart grid, and industrial automation.
With a workforce of over 100,000 people and over 50 years of experience helping our customers to solve their power problems, ABB has invested more than USD 11 billion in research and development in our research facilities in more than 20 countries, putting us among the top in the world in our innovation. We launch products and upgrades for customers annually, with thousands of new product launches in almost all of our product categories. Our broad, integrated portfolio covers a wide spectrum of electrification, including traditional, renewable, transportation, distributed, and industrial electrification.
To learn more about ABB, please visit abb.com.
